VERDICT: PASS -- OSPFv2 on the x960-56YSQ is gated behind `service ospf`, forms Full
adjacencies with two neighbours over two interfaces, installs routes the protocol
itself carried (code O, AD 110, each prefix traced to the owning partner's Router LSA
in the link-state database) for destinations reachable no other way, and forwards over
them on the wire; withdrawing one advertisement stops that forwarding while the second
neighbour keeps forwarding in the same leg.
      service gate, before anything ......... `show ip ospf` refused; no ospf line in
                                              running-config; no OSPF route
      gate is real and asynchronous ......... `router ospf` rejected ~1 s after
                                              `service ospf`, accepted within 7 s
      adjacencies ........................... 2.2.2.2 and 3.3.3.3 both Full/DR, 17 s
                                              after `router ospf 1` completed
      route learned from the protocol ....... O 10.70.70.1/32 [110/2] via 10.0.61.2,
                                              O 10.90.90.1/32 [110/2] via 10.0.41.2;
                                              `show running-config | include ip route`
                                              empty throughout
      which neighbour advertised it ......... each loopback carried by the Router LSA
                                              originated by the partner that owns it
      forwarding over the learned routes .... 5/5 and 5/5 echo replies, each sourced by
                                              the loopback under test
      control flow, same leg ................ 203.0.113.9 0/5 in every single leg
      instrument control, same leg .......... 192.168.10.1 5/5 in every single leg
      it is version 2 on the wire ........... OSPFv2 Hello, proto 89, to 224.0.0.5,
                                              Backbone Area, timers 10/40
      withdrawal, proven on the wire ........ 5/5 -> 0/5 in under 7 s with the port, the
                                              link and the adjacency all still up, and
                                              swi_b's Router LSA re-originated with one
                                              fewer link; re-advertising restored 5/5
      AD 110 loses to a static at AD 1 ...... in the DATAPLANE: 5 ICMP time-exceeded
                                              sourced by the static next hop 10.0.41.2
      interface cost changes the metric ..... `ip ospf cost 50` moved [110/2] -> [110/51]
                                              on that route only
      passive-interface, both claims ........ 0 OSPF packets in 30 s against one Hello
                                              per 10 s, while the neighbour still holds
                                              192.168.10.0 as a stub link in the DUT's
                                              Router LSA; user traffic 5/5 throughout
      removal ............................... `no router ospf 1` returns the dataplane
                                              to the step-0 baseline, capture for capture
      persistence across a real reboot ...... 61 s reload; config, service gate, both
                                              adjacencies, both routes and forwarding
                                              all return unaided
CAVEAT:  Single backbone area 0.0.0.0 only. Inter-area routing, ABR/ASBR behaviour,
         stub and NSSA areas and route summarisation were not exercised. `redistribute`
         into OSPF and `default-information originate` were not exercised. OSPF
         authentication was not exercised -- the wire capture shows Authentication Type:
         none (0), which is the default. Route filtering, distribute-lists and
         route-maps in OSPF were not exercised. `ip ospf cost` was proven to change the
         METRIC, but each loopback has exactly one way in on this bench, so cost was not
         shown to MOVE traffic, and OSPF equal-cost multipath could not be exercised for
         the same reason. swi_b's OSPF-64 route limit was nowhere near approached.

