STEP 0 -- baseline: OSPF off, and the service gate read first                    done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: read the DUT's state with no `service ospf` and no `router ospf` anywhere,
  then run a full counted leg, so the later steps are interpretable against it.

  State, 21:35:46-21:35:52:

awplus# show ip ospf
  % OSPF protocol daemon is not running or feature license is not available
awplus# show ip ospf neighbor
  % OSPF protocol daemon is not running or feature license is not available
awplus# show ip route ospf
  Gateway of last resort is not set
  No entries in route table
awplus# show running-config | include ospf
awplus#                                    <-- EMPTY: no service, no router process, no
                                               interface command
awplus# show arp
  IP Address      LL Address       Interface            Port        Type
awplus#                                    <-- EMPTY

  That refusal message conflates two different causes -- "daemon is not running" OR
  "feature license is not available". This DUT holds OSPF-FULL, so on this unit it can
  only be the daemon, and STEP 1 settles it constructively: `service ospf` alone makes
  the same command answer. No limb of this case is graded UNSUPPORTED on the strength
  of that message.

  STP immediately before the leg (21:35:51):
