  The DUT emitted 2 ICMP type 3 destination-unreachables from its own vlan10 address,
  so it made and reported a routing decision rather than silently blackholing. Only 2
  for 15 unroutable packets: unreachable generation is rate-limited here, so their
  SOURCE is attribution and their COUNT is not a measurement. The ABSENCE of echo
  replies from the two loopbacks is the measurement.

  => STEP 0 done: with OSPF off neither partner loopback is reachable, the control is
     dropped and the instrument answers 5/5. Everything measured later is against this.

STEP 1 -- enable OSPFv2, form adjacencies, and forward over a protocol-learned route
                                                                                 PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: enable the service and the routing process on all three devices, advertise
  each partner's loopback, then count a leg to prefixes for which no static route
  exists anywhere.

  1a. THE SERVICE GATE IS REAL, AND IT IS NOT INSTANT. `service ospf` and `router ospf`
  cannot go in the same console batch. Measured on all three devices:

x960-28YSQ(config)# service ospf                    21:36:59
x960-28YSQ(config)# router ospf 1                   21:37:00  (+1 s)
  % OSPF protocol daemon is not running or feature license is not available
awplus(config)# service ospf                        21:37:08  (swi_a, same at +1 s)

  Re-checked on swi_b at 21:37:23, with nothing else done:

x960-28YSQ# show ip ospf
  OSPF Routing Process not enabled.        <-- the DAEMON is up; no router process yet
x960-28YSQ# show running-config | include service ospf
  service ospf

  Timed on the DUT: `service ospf` at 21:38:16; the first poll at 21:38:23 (+7 s)
  already read `OSPF Routing Process not enabled.`, i.e. the daemon was up. The window
  in which `router ospf` is rejected is therefore LONGER THAN 1 s AND SHORTER THAN 7 s
  after `service ospf`. Both partners took `router ospf 1` without error when it was
  re-sent at 21:37:42 and 21:37:53. The licence half of the refusal message is ruled
  out: the DUT holds OSPF-FULL, and the command succeeded seconds later with no licence
  change.

  1b. CONFIGURATION APPLIED, quoted exactly as sent:

    swi_b (/dev/u3) 21:37:41-21:37:45        swi_a (/dev/u5) 21:37:52-21:37:56
