  No command was rejected. Router-ids are set explicitly (1.1.1.1 DUT, 2.2.2.2 swi_b,
  3.3.3.3 swi_a) so every later read-back names the neighbour unambiguously instead of
  inheriting an interface address. The guide's syntax (C613-22055-00 REV E p.3,
  "To enter OSPF configuration mode, type in:" -- `configure terminal` / `service ospf`
  / `router ospf 1`, and p.12's prefix form of `network`) was followed as printed.

