      Options [External]
        Hello Timer 10s, Dead Timer 40s, Mask 255.255.255.0, Priority 1
        Designated Router 192.168.10.1
  (second Hello 11.0 s later, 21:41:40.187571 -- the 10 s hello timer, measured)

  => STEP 1 PASS: the service gate is a real, asynchronous gate and not a platform gap;
     both adjacencies reach Full in 17 s; the DUT installs O / AD 110 routes for two
     prefixes while `show running-config | include ip route` stays empty, each traced
     in the LSDB to the Router LSA of the partner that owns it; and 5/5 plus 5/5 echo
     replies sourced by those loopbacks prove end-to-end forwarding over routes that
     exist only because OSPF put them there -- with the control dropped and the
     instrument alive in the same leg. The wire capture ties the case title to what the
     DUT emits: OSPFv2, protocol 89, to 224.0.0.5, area 0.0.0.0, timers 10/40.

